+/* A continuation is forth.rkt's (λ () (cps-code code (add1 i) k)), a closure {ip, k, fn}, and
+ * it takes one cell. Nodes are pushed and popped in LIFO order, so k is always the next cell
+ * up and need not be stored. ip is 8-byte aligned, so its low 3 bits are free to hold fn,
+ * an index into fns[]: 0 is resume, and a cell that is just an ip, which is what DOCOL
+ * pushes and what jonesforth leaves on its return stack, already has fn = 0. The chain is
+ * therefore the return-stack array: RSP@ is a real address, `8+` steps to the parent, and
+ * jonesforth.f's THROW walks it unmodified. Calling a continuation is still a tail call
+ * through fn.
+ * ponytail: a continuation that outlived its caller (call/cc) would need k stored again. */
